WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:54.010
<b>Klabautermann</b>

3
00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:55.570
[WORKMAN]
Fire!

4
00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:57.900
Emergency! Everybody wake up!

5
00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:01.700
Damn them! Those pirates
started this, didn't they?!

6
00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:02.970
We need to do something, quick!

7
00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:04.780
There are still a lot
of people left inside!

8
00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:07.810
Iceburg might be trapped!
Let's make sure he made it out!

9
00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:09.850
Right! Come on!

10
00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:13.780
The rest of you...
put out that fire! Go! Go!

11
00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:25.670
[LUCCI]
It appears the fire is beginning to spread.

12
00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:31.840
Leopard. Human.
Whatever the hell you are.

13
00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:35.610
You're not gonna lay one
finger on Iceburg. You hear me?!

14
00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:39.520
No! He's a Carnivore Zoan-type!

15
00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:41.520
They're the most brutal of them all!

16
00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:47.100
Indeed. Logia types.
Zoan types. Paramythia types.

17
00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:50.400
Each one extremely powerful in their own unique way.

18
00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:53.840
The ability to enhance one's
own personal strength happens

19
00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:56.110
to be the specialty
of the Zoan type.

20
00:02:56.730 --> 00:03:00.410
In other words, the more we train, the stronger we get.

21
00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:03.100
Which makes the Zoan
type the most lethal

22
00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:06.110
when it comes to
attacks at close range.

23
00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:08.290
[WORKMAN]
Go! Move it!

24
00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:12.840
[KALIFA]
Lucci. The workmen are
making their way up the stairs.

25
00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:16.400
[LUCCI]
Don't worry.
They'll never make it this far.

26
00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:18.340
Tempest Kick!

27
00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:31.490
[WORKMAN]
Go back!
The ceiling's collapsing!

28
00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:34.460
[WORKMEN shouting]

29
00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:43.400
[CHOPPER]
Nami!

30
00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.940
Chopper!

31
00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:55.110
[ICEBURG]
What are you doing?

32
00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:57.380
[PAULIE]
No matter what, I'm getting you out of here!

33
00:03:57.410 --> 00:04:00.110
[ICEBURG]
There's no way!
Your wounds are far too...

34
00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:04.280
[KALIFA]
I'm afraid we can't let you do that.

35
00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:12.220
And I'm afraid,
you're gonna have to!

36
00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:20.680
Damn you! Why did it
have to be you guys?!

37
00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:26.620
No. I can't believe you.

38
00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:28.420
How could you do this?!

39
00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:32.020
You tricked me!
I thought you were my friends!

40
00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:38.130
[LUCCI]
Then you were mistaken.

41
00:04:49.730 --> 00:04:52.150
[LUFFY]
Talking pigeon jerk!

42
00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:54.110
Luffy, what are you...?!

43
00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:01.750
[LUCCI]
Finger Pistol.

44
00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:04.120
Luffy!

45
00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:30.730
Have a nice flight!

46
00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:37.630
[NAMI]
Luffy!

47
00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:39.200
Damn you!

48
00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:42.560
[LUCCI]
Iron Body!

49
00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.130
[NAMI]
Zoro!

50
00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:11.610
Now it's your turn.

51
00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:30.260
Did everyone make it out?

52
00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:33.230
[WORKMAN]
It's taken the building.
We can't go back inside.

53
00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:35.830
Have each team check to see if anyone's missing!

54
00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:39.700
Hey! Have you heard anything
about Iceburg? Is he safe?

55
00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:42.330
Don't tell me. He's not
stuck in there, is he?

56
00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:44.400
Of course not!
The foremen are with him.

57
00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:46.100
There's no way
they left him behind.

58
00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:48.970
Search the area! I'm sure
he's here somewhere!

59
00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:59.350
Hey, wait. That woman's one of
the Straw Hats! I'm sure of it!

60
00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:01.920
Did she jump out from one of the windows?

61
00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:04.000
She probably got
trapped by the fire

62
00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:06.270
and didn't have any
other choice in the matter.

63
00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:08.290
Well, what should we do with her?

64
00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:11.240
These damn pirates have
done a terrible thing here.

65
00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:14.110
Let's make her tell us where the rest of her crew is!

66
00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:17.150
We'll hunt them down and turn them over to the Navy!

67
00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:24.110
[LUCCI]
The testimony of a pirate won't hold up as evidence.

68
00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:28.660
This case will remain a mystery.

69
00:07:28.690 --> 00:07:32.960
Iceburg. No matter how great of
a shipbuilding engineer you are,

70
00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:36.700
no matter how great a mayor.

71
00:07:36.730 --> 00:07:38.640
A mere individual
citizen shouldn't

72
00:07:38.670 --> 00:07:41.110
oppose the World Government.

73
00:07:50.050 --> 00:07:53.280
Let's go. We need to
find Tom's other apprentice,

74
00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:56.350
Franky or rather Cutty Flam,

75
00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:58.660
and take those
blueprints away from him.

76
00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:16.570
Granny! Granny!
There's a huge fire!

77
00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:21.440
[KOKORO]
It's Galley-La's main office.
Such a terrible thing to do.

78
00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:24.620
What do you mean, Granny?

79
00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:26.450
Did someone start the fire on purpose?

80
00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:29.250
Well, I can't really say for sure.

81
00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:31.690
But usually, when I
get a bad feeling,

82
00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:33.480
it turns out to be right.

83
00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:36.420
I sure hope that
Iceburg is doing okay.

84
00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:39.680
Seriously.

85
00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:42.190
All this is happening
over that thing.

86
00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:44.260
It shouldn't even exist.

87
00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:58.040
You're sure of it?

88
00:08:58.070 --> 00:09:00.880
You saw Franky wandering
into your bar earlier?

89
00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:02.580
[BLUENO]
Yeah. I spoke with him.

90
00:09:02.610 --> 00:09:04.680
But he took off to go look for Straw Hat.

91
00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:07.740
[LUCCI]
I see.

92
00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:11.920
Seems like he doesn't stay in one place for very long.

93
00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:16.850
Wow. Some people just have
the worst sense of timing.

94
00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:18.740
[KAKU]
Look there.

95
00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:22.880
[UNDERLING]
Listen up, Straw Hat!
We've got Long Nose!

96
00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:25.000
That's right!
We totally have him!

97
00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:27.650
If you don't want him to sing in the key of C!

98
00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:30.800
You idiot! How many times
do I have to tell you?!

99
00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:32.940
It's "If you don't want
him to sink into the sea"!

100
00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:33.920
Drink some iced tea!

101
00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:35.910
The sea! Are you deaf?

102
00:09:35.940 --> 00:09:37.980
What kind of a threat is that?
It doesn't make any sense!

103
00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:39.250
Whatever!

104
00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:41.080
All that matters is getting
the message to Straw Hat.

105
00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:43.160
Giving him that stupid message won't do any good!

106
00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:45.630
And bro Franky will end up kicking your butt!

107
00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:47.370
[ZAMBAI]
"If you don't want him sunk
to the bottom of the sea,

108
00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:49.100
go to the warehouse
under the bridge.

109
00:09:49.140 --> 00:09:52.710
With regards, Franky"!
Like that!

110
00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:54.680
If he gets the message
and he does come,

111
00:09:54.710 --> 00:09:57.110
Bro is gonna beat the
living crap outta him!

112
00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:01.820
[LUCCI]
Who did you say
is waiting for whom,

113
00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:03.860
and where is this
certain someone waiting?

114
00:10:03.890 --> 00:10:06.030
[ZAMBAI]
Huh? Who the hell are you?

115
00:10:06.060 --> 00:10:08.800
We're kind of busy
right now. Get lost!

116
00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:09.860
If you want to live,

117
00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:13.100
you'll answer my question
in the next 3 seconds.

118
00:10:13.190 --> 00:10:15.860
Huh?!

119
00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:18.000
Is that some kinda'
joke, you nut-job?

120
00:10:18.030 --> 00:10:19.980
Do you even have
the slightest clue

121
00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:21.550
as to what family
we're a part of?

122
00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:27.020
[LUCCI]
What did you mean by "the
warehouse under the bridge"?

123
00:10:27.110 --> 00:10:29.840
Is that the place where Franky is?

124
00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:34.050
Whatever business
you have with Franky

125
00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:38.010
is gonna have to go
through us first. Right guys?!

126
00:10:40.580 --> 00:10:43.500
<b>Main Bridge Opposite the Garbage Dump
Northeast Shore, the Narrows, Water Seven</b>

127
00:10:41.980 --> 00:10:45.980
[FRANKY crying]

128
00:10:43.540 --> 00:10:45.960
<b>A Warehouse Under the Bridge
(Franky's Secret Base)</b>

129
00:10:51.970 --> 00:10:53.970
[MOZU crying]

130
00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:55.440
[KIWI]
To think that you left the
friends you traveled here

131
00:10:55.470 --> 00:10:58.210
with all the way from the
East Blue for your ship!

132
00:10:58.240 --> 00:11:02.110
Why in the world are the three of you crying about it?

133
00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:04.460
[FRANKY]
What?! We're not
crying, you idiot!

134
00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:07.020
I was just thinking about
everything you've been through

135
00:11:07.070 --> 00:11:10.210
to protect that ship all
alone and it touched my heart!

136
00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:13.910
[KIWI and MOZU]
– We're not crying! None of us are crying! Really!
– We're not crying! None of us are crying! Really!

137
00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:16.320
What the heck is wrong with these nitwits?

138
00:11:16.350 --> 00:11:18.350
[FRANKY ET AL. crying]

139
00:11:18.180 --> 00:11:20.280
Anyway, you get the gist of it, right?

140
00:11:20.310 --> 00:11:21.810
We're no longer friends!

141
00:11:21.810 --> 00:11:23.920
The Straw Hats are part of my past now!

142
00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:26.150
It's so sad.

143
00:11:26.180 --> 00:11:28.590
So sad that I'll have to sing about it!

144
00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:32.020
This song is called, "Severed
Friendship! North Wind Chop!"

145
00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:33.990
Yeah! Sing it, bro!

146
00:11:34.120 --> 00:11:36.090
Hey! Are you
making fun of me?!

147
00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:47.000
[FRANKY]
Is the tea ready yet?
I'm dying of thirst over here!

148
00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:50.170
[KIWI and MOZU]
– Almost! We'll bring it over in just a moment!
– Almost! We'll bring it over in just a moment!

149
00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:55.460
That crying wore me out.
Not that I really cried.

150
00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:03.250
[KIWI]
Here you go, bro. Now be
careful, it's really hot!

151
00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:07.250
Thank you so much!

152
00:12:07.290 --> 00:12:10.520
Okay, I understand what's what, brother.

153
00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:12.560
[blowing]
[slurping tea]

154
00:12:13.020 --> 00:12:14.060
Hot!

155
00:12:14.090 --> 00:12:16.260
She just got through
telling you that! Calm down!

156
00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:19.830
Sorry about that, bro. You okay?

157
00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:22.390
[MOZU]
Why don't you take a break
and have some tea, as well?

158
00:12:27.110 --> 00:12:28.880
[FRANKY]
I can't blame you.

159
00:12:28.910 --> 00:12:31.610
You must be holding quite the grudge against us.

160
00:12:31.650 --> 00:12:35.520
You know, since we stole your 200 million berries and all.

161
00:12:35.550 --> 00:12:36.680
Especially because it led

162
00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:39.490
to such a big fight
with your captain.

163
00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:42.410
[USOPP]
Whatever.
What happens, happens.

164
00:12:42.410 --> 00:12:45.540
No sense in holding
a grudge about it.

165
00:12:45.560 --> 00:12:51.970
Taking the high road.
How manly. About that money.

166
00:12:52.030 --> 00:12:54.570
I spent all of it!

167
00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:56.540
I'm gonna knock you flat.

168
00:12:56.540 --> 00:12:59.080
[FRANKY]
Now, now.
Don't get so worked up!

169
00:12:59.110 --> 00:13:00.840
Especially after you showed me

170
00:13:00.910 --> 00:13:03.480
how dignified and
forgiving you are!

171
00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:07.650
Come on, brother! Can't we
just let bygones be bygones?

172
00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:09.650
I mean, I haven't
flipped out on you

173
00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:13.020
for destroying my home and
demolition factory, have I?

174
00:13:13.050 --> 00:13:16.760
And on top of that, you guys
annihilated my subordinates...

175
00:13:16.790 --> 00:13:18.760
You bastards!
How dare you? I'll kill you!

176
00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:19.730
[MOZU]
Easy, bro!

177
00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:21.630
[KIWI]
You gotta control that anger!

178
00:13:34.780 --> 00:13:37.550
Yep. A lot has happened
these past few days.

179
00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:40.180
But I do think we're better
off putting it all behind us.

180
00:13:40.220 --> 00:13:41.780
So what do you say
we just put the axe

181
00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:43.720
in the ground
and call it a day?

182
00:13:43.750 --> 00:13:45.560
I think you mean
"bury the hatchet."

183
00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:48.720
Yeah. I'm pretty sure it's
"bury the hatchet," bro.

184
00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:50.550
So what's next?

185
00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:52.680
What will you do now that you're on your own?

186
00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:55.110
It doesn't seem like you have anywhere to go.

187
00:13:55.360 --> 00:13:56.220
Tell you what.

188
00:13:56.260 --> 00:13:57.960
Why don't you let
me take care of you?

189
00:13:57.990 --> 00:14:00.090
Join The Franky Family!

190
00:14:00.130 --> 00:14:02.060
You seem like a good man,
and I could always...

191
00:14:02.100 --> 00:14:06.100
[USOPP]
Forget it! I have no plans
to become a ship dismantler.

192
00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:08.280
Even though I'm no
longer a Straw Hat,

193
00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:10.120
I'm still a pirate! Got it?

194
00:14:11.190 --> 00:14:14.670
You've moved me to song.
This is "The Pirate Code."

195
00:14:14.670 --> 00:14:16.640
[KIWI and MOZU]
– Yeah! Sing it, bro!
– Yeah! Sing it, bro!

196
00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:19.870
Don't sing it, and I still
think you're making fun of me!

197
00:14:19.910 --> 00:14:22.200
[FRANKY]
Look, I'm just concerned, that's all.

198
00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:24.600
I'm thinking about your future.

199
00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:26.170
[USOPP]
My future is none
of your business!

200
00:14:26.200 --> 00:14:28.700
And besides, there
are other things

201
00:14:28.740 --> 00:14:30.440
you should be concerned
with right now.

202
00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:32.680
Like that huge
storm headed this way.

203
00:14:32.710 --> 00:14:35.610
True. But we're safe here.

204
00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:37.810
Aqua Laguna can be pretty devastating.

205
00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:40.020
When it hits, we all have to pull together.

206
00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:43.470
Starting now until
late into the night,

207
00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:45.940
houses will be submerged
up to the second floor.

208
00:14:45.970 --> 00:14:47.500
If you're stuck in
the backstreets

209
00:14:47.540 --> 00:14:50.040
or capes during that time,
you don't stand a chance.

210
00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:51.840
But this area's safe.

211
00:14:51.880 --> 00:14:54.680
Your ship will be safe too,
if you wanna keep it here.

212
00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:58.300
Oh. Thank you very much.
I really appreciate it.

213
00:14:58.300 --> 00:15:00.400
[FRANKY]
Stop acting like we're strangers, moron!

214
00:15:00.430 --> 00:15:02.400
[USOPP]
I imagine it must be
tough having to deal with

215
00:15:02.410 --> 00:15:04.510
this storm and the chaos
it causes every year.

216
00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:06.340
[FRANKY]
Nah. It's not so bad.

217
00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:09.380
We've all gotten used to the annual evacuation.

218
00:15:09.410 --> 00:15:11.410
The real problem is the water level.

219
00:15:11.440 --> 00:15:15.350
It increases little by little every single year.

220
00:15:15.380 --> 00:15:17.920
The back streets you
see all through Water Seven

221
00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:20.290
are built on the
rooftops of an old town

222
00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:23.570
that existed several hundred years ago.

223
00:15:23.600 --> 00:15:25.640
It's said that the
shipbuilding island

224
00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:28.080
and the backstreets used to be
part of the same piece of land.

225
00:15:28.120 --> 00:15:31.020
But now, so much of it has sunk under the sea.

226
00:15:31.050 --> 00:15:33.720
That's why they call
it a "floating city."

227
00:15:33.790 --> 00:15:36.830
All of the sidewalks
became canals and waterways.

228
00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:38.920
[MOZU]
If you want to be
more precise about it:

229
00:15:38.970 --> 00:15:40.100
Technically,

230
00:15:40.140 --> 00:15:41.210
rather than saying that the
water level is increasing,

231
00:15:41.240 --> 00:15:43.610
the foundation of the
island is actually sinking.

232
00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:44.930
[KIWI]
If it keeps up,

233
00:15:44.930 --> 00:15:47.870
the city will become harder
and harder to live in.

234
00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:51.500
[USOPP]
I see. Even this
beautiful city of water has

235
00:15:51.500 --> 00:15:54.270
its share of hardships
too, doesn't it?

236
00:15:54.280 --> 00:15:57.410
Hmm... But still.
If push comes to shove,

237
00:15:57.450 --> 00:15:58.550
you can just take the Sea Train

238
00:15:58.580 --> 00:16:00.520
and go live
somewhere else, right?

239
00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:04.250
You can say that now.
But not always.

240
00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:06.390
It's only been around for ten years.

241
00:16:06.420 --> 00:16:08.890
Before that time, you were totally out of luck.

242
00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:11.530
Getting across the ocean
without it is no easy task,

243
00:16:11.560 --> 00:16:13.560
even if you have a boat.

244
00:16:15.560 --> 00:16:16.500
[FRANKY]
This island is isolated.

245
00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:19.290
There was never much traffic to or from it.

246
00:16:19.350 --> 00:16:21.780
The people who lived here
carried with them the looming

247
00:16:21.820 --> 00:16:24.790
fear that someday this entire
city and everything around it

248
00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:28.260
would sink into the sea.
They became hopeless.

249
00:16:29.110 --> 00:16:31.450
[train whistle]

250
00:16:39.610 --> 00:16:41.980
The one thing that
finally took away

251
00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:45.570
that fear was the
Sea Train, The Puffing Tom.

252
00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:47.880
[MOZU]
Now, anyone at
any time can travel

253
00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:49.750
across the sea
without a Log Pose.

254
00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:52.690
This was a huge
step for the island!

255
00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:55.740
And we owe everything to one man.

256
00:16:55.770 --> 00:16:59.840
A brilliant shipwright named
Tom who created that Sea Train.

257
00:16:59.880 --> 00:17:04.380
He saved us all.
And gave this island new life.

258
00:17:12.220 --> 00:17:14.100
Bro!

259
00:17:14.600 --> 00:17:16.600
[punches landing]

260
00:17:17.490 --> 00:17:19.730
[ZAMBAI]
Help me.

261
00:17:24.390 --> 00:17:27.870
[LUCCI]
I'll say hello to your "bro"
for you when we pay him a visit.

262
00:17:38.960 --> 00:17:40.460
We now know the location.

263
00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:46.210
Let's go.

264
00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:13.450
[FRANKY]
Hey! Gotta question
for you, brother.

265
00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:16.590
I'll just get right to the point.

266
00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:19.460
What are you gonna do after you fix that ship?

267
00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:21.630
[USOPP]
Uh... Well, let's see.

268
00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:24.060
First, we'll go on a
few adventures together,

269
00:18:24.100 --> 00:18:25.200
and eventually I'll sail her

270
00:18:25.230 --> 00:18:27.540
back to our home in the East Blue.

271
00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:30.540
I know we didn't sail
around the world or anything.

272
00:18:30.570 --> 00:18:33.070
But the Merry and I made it
all the way to the Grand Line!

273
00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:34.740
I'd call that a
successful voyage

274
00:18:34.770 --> 00:18:36.670
that will end with
a triumphant return!

275
00:18:36.700 --> 00:18:37.640
So, with our heads held high...

276
00:18:37.700 --> 00:18:40.540
[FRANKY]
Nope. Sorry, not gonna happen.

277
00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:42.960
You can't go all the way back to the East Blue.

278
00:18:43.750 --> 00:18:45.810
It's too far away.

279
00:18:50.300 --> 00:18:52.070
[MOZU]
What do you mean?

280
00:18:52.870 --> 00:18:55.010
I took a close
look at your ship

281
00:18:55.040 --> 00:18:56.880
when we were bringing
it up here earlier.

282
00:18:56.910 --> 00:18:59.080
Got to see her from every angle.

283
00:18:59.190 --> 00:19:01.360
[FRANKY]
That ship is at the end of her life.

284
00:19:01.390 --> 00:19:04.400
Galley-La's assessment was correct.

285
00:19:04.430 --> 00:19:06.570
As an expert in the
demolition business,

286
00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:08.540
I suggest you dismantle her.

287
00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:10.920
[USOPP]
What? That's ridiculous!

288
00:19:11.300 --> 00:19:15.270
I'll even help you do the job.
Like I said, I'm an expert.

289
00:19:15.280 --> 00:19:16.290
Are you crazy?

290
00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:19.430
What in the hell are you
talking about, you jerk?!

291
00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:23.500
Hold on! Don't come any
closer! Stop! I mean it!

292
00:19:23.530 --> 00:19:24.940
[KIWI and MOZU]
– Bro!
– Bro!

293
00:19:24.960 --> 00:19:26.160
Take it easy!

294
00:19:26.200 --> 00:19:28.430
I'm simply offering to help demolish this ship, that's all.

295
00:19:28.460 --> 00:19:30.170
[USOPP]
Stop screwing around!

296
00:19:30.300 --> 00:19:32.770
I'm not gonna let you
anywhere near her, understand?!

297
00:19:32.950 --> 00:19:35.320
Get lost!
The Merry is my ship!

298
00:19:36.140 --> 00:19:38.600
[FRANKY]
You're wrong. Listen.

299
00:19:38.610 --> 00:19:41.510
That old girl's no longer a ship.

300
00:19:42.870 --> 00:19:44.370
What'd you say?

301
00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:47.010
Earlier, I asked you a question.

302
00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:50.120
About what you planned on doing once you fixed that ship.

303
00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:51.290
Now if you had said that

304
00:19:51.320 --> 00:19:52.690
you were going to
cast away your life

305
00:19:52.720 --> 00:19:55.220
to the sea and go down
along with her, then.

306
00:19:55.350 --> 00:19:58.090
Well, I wouldn't have had anything to say about it.

307
00:19:58.270 --> 00:19:59.300
No questions.

308
00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:03.450
But since you just told
me that you plan on going

309
00:20:03.520 --> 00:20:05.450
all the way back to
the East Blue with her.

310
00:20:05.490 --> 00:20:09.660
Well. Now I have
to stop you, brother.

311
00:20:11.790 --> 00:20:13.860
That ship is at her end.

312
00:20:13.930 --> 00:20:17.560
She won't even make it
to the next island. Listen.

313
00:20:17.560 --> 00:20:20.300
A ship is born with one promise.

314
00:20:20.330 --> 00:20:23.330
"To carry you across the sea
from one shore to another."

315
00:20:23.360 --> 00:20:27.760
That's her sole purpose.
The reason for her existence.

316
00:20:27.800 --> 00:20:30.260
Which means, when the time comes

317
00:20:30.260 --> 00:20:33.190
that a ship can no longer
carry you across the sea.

318
00:20:36.260 --> 00:20:39.260
Hey! Stop! No!

319
00:20:39.290 --> 00:20:41.460
Then that promise
has been broken,

320
00:20:41.500 --> 00:20:45.670
and she's no longer a ship!

321
00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:47.270
[KIWI and MOZU]
– Bro!
– Bro!

322
00:20:53.650 --> 00:20:57.780
No! Stop it!

323
00:21:08.540 --> 00:21:12.540
You bastard! Keep
away from the Merry!

324
00:21:23.630 --> 00:21:25.860
Son of a bitch!

325
00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:30.190
If you don't understand...

326
00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:40.110
[FRANKY]
Then take a look with
your own damn eyes!

327
00:24:24.590 --> 00:24:26.670
Sorry, Merry.

328
00:24:29.850 --> 00:24:32.250
Don't worry.

329
00:24:32.290 --> 00:24:35.660
I'll fix you up
right away. Every time.

330
00:24:35.690 --> 00:24:41.230
As many times as you
need. No matter what.

331
00:24:41.260 --> 00:24:45.500
I'll always take care
of you! Always!

332
00:24:48.620 --> 00:24:50.620
[KIWI and MOZU sobbing]

333
00:24:50.400 --> 00:24:51.270
Hey!

334
00:24:51.300 --> 00:24:52.910
Enough already, Long Nose!

335
00:24:52.920 --> 00:24:54.800
You saw the bottom
of the ship, right?!

336
00:24:55.360 --> 00:24:57.310
The keel is broken
right down the middle!

337
00:24:57.310 --> 00:25:00.220
The outer panels are slipping
off, and the frame is shot!

338
00:25:00.220 --> 00:25:03.390
With a hull like that, the
first wave would rip her apart!

339
00:25:03.480 --> 00:25:06.000
And you think that a
complete amateur like you

340
00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:07.700
can just grab a hammer and...

341
00:25:15.510 --> 00:25:18.010
You shut your damn mouth!

342
00:25:18.050 --> 00:25:20.520
I don't wanna hear
another word out of you!

343
00:25:20.550 --> 00:25:23.950
If you so much as breathe,
I'll kick your teeth in!

344
00:25:23.980 --> 00:25:25.220
You hear me?!

345
00:25:28.180 --> 00:25:30.180
[USOPP sniffling]

346
00:25:50.410 --> 00:25:51.610
Besides, I already knew.

347
00:25:51.610 --> 00:25:51.910
To be honest. In my heart.

348
00:25:51.910 --> 00:25:56.670
I knew it all along.

349
00:25:56.670 --> 00:25:58.810
I knew the truth!

350
00:25:58.840 --> 00:26:01.440
I knew that the Merry
was at the end of her life!

351
00:26:08.200 --> 00:26:13.470
[USOPP]
Deep down, I... I knew it.

352
00:26:14.120 --> 00:26:18.160
When I heard the assessment.
I knew that what I saw

353
00:26:18.190 --> 00:26:21.460
on that day back in
Skypia really happened.

354
00:26:23.120 --> 00:26:26.840
At first, I thought I was dreaming.

355
00:26:27.840 --> 00:26:31.170
That there was no way it could be real.

356
00:26:31.940 --> 00:26:35.780
On one foggy night in
a forest lit with nothing

357
00:26:35.810 --> 00:26:37.810
but moonlight I heard

358
00:26:37.850 --> 00:26:40.320
the hammering strikes
of a wooden mallet.

359
00:26:40.350 --> 00:26:43.390
It sounded like it was coming
from the direction of the ship

360
00:26:43.420 --> 00:26:47.470
but at the time there shouldn't
have been anybody on board.

361
00:26:47.470 --> 00:26:50.000
I crept closer and

362
00:26:50.160 --> 00:26:53.630
confirmed the sound was
indeed coming from the Merry.

363
00:26:53.660 --> 00:26:57.200
The fog was thick but
I'm sure I saw someone there

364
00:26:57.230 --> 00:26:59.570
striking away
with a wooden mallet.

365
00:26:59.680 --> 00:27:02.780
I... I couldn't figure out who it was.

366
00:27:05.460 --> 00:27:06.550
[LUFFY]
Whoa! Check it out!
This is amazing!

367
00:27:06.550 --> 00:27:07.720
[USOPP]
On the morning of the next day.

368
00:27:07.760 --> 00:27:11.960
We awoke to find the ship
had been haphazardly repaired.

369
00:27:12.030 --> 00:27:16.140
Even the broken mast was back where it had always been.

370
00:27:16.170 --> 00:27:18.310
But there was something
even more peculiar

371
00:27:18.340 --> 00:27:21.010
that was bugging me.

372
00:27:21.140 --> 00:27:23.340
Whoever fixed the Merry
knew how she used to look.

373
00:27:23.340 --> 00:27:26.150
Despite all of the
modifications we'd made to her,

374
00:27:26.180 --> 00:27:27.720
this mysterious person

375
00:27:27.750 --> 00:27:30.010
had brought her back
to her original shape.

376
00:27:30.010 --> 00:27:31.580
She was still in
rough condition,

377
00:27:31.610 --> 00:27:36.420
but she was the same old
Merry she had been before.

378
00:27:36.460 --> 00:27:38.560
The whole situation remained a mystery.

379
00:27:38.600 --> 00:27:42.370
But for some reason, these words lingered in my heart.

380
00:27:42.400 --> 00:27:44.300
I don't know if it's
something I actually heard

381
00:27:44.330 --> 00:27:47.870
someone say or maybe
just something I'd imagined.

382
00:27:49.420 --> 00:27:50.480
[BOY]
Don't worry.

383
00:27:53.600 --> 00:27:56.200
I'll carry everyone for a little bit longer.

384
00:27:58.940 --> 00:28:02.840
I know it sounds
ridiculous but I...

385
00:28:02.950 --> 00:28:07.320
I think it was an
incarnation of the Merry.

386
00:28:07.500 --> 00:28:10.030
And she spoke to me.

387
00:28:12.740 --> 00:28:14.740
[USOPP sniffling]

388
00:28:14.140 --> 00:28:17.280
[USOPP]
She probably already knew that she was at her limits.

389
00:28:17.320 --> 00:28:20.980
And so she appeared in that form to tell us.

390
00:28:21.020 --> 00:28:25.560
She wanted to reassure us that it'd be all right.

391
00:28:25.820 --> 00:28:26.990
That's what I thought of

392
00:28:26.990 --> 00:28:29.460
when I heard her
assessment from Galley-La.

393
00:28:31.590 --> 00:28:33.590
[sniffling]

394
00:28:33.430 --> 00:28:35.600
You think I'm completely out of my mind, don't you?

395
00:28:35.630 --> 00:28:38.340
I don't care... You don't
have to believe me.

396
00:28:40.470 --> 00:28:42.440
What is it, Bro?

397
00:28:42.470 --> 00:28:44.310
[FRANKY]
Whether I believe it or not.

398
00:28:44.440 --> 00:28:47.280
You said that
whoever it was you saw

399
00:28:47.310 --> 00:28:50.280
looked like someone holding
a wooden mallet, right?

400
00:28:50.320 --> 00:28:54.720
That's right.
Does it mean something?

401
00:28:54.760 --> 00:28:59.730
Yeah, it sure does. It means
that you saw a Klabautermann.

402
00:28:59.920 --> 00:29:02.190
Kla... Klabau-what?

403
00:29:03.180 --> 00:29:05.520
A Klabautermann.

404
00:29:05.730 --> 00:29:08.700
It's an old legend that's passed down from sailor to sailor.

405
00:29:08.700 --> 00:29:11.200
It's a very particular type of fairy.

406
00:29:11.200 --> 00:29:14.100
It only dwells on ships treated with great care.

407
00:29:14.140 --> 00:29:17.270
You could say it's the ship's spirit.

408
00:29:18.440 --> 00:29:21.310
It's said that it carries a
wooden mallet in its hand

409
00:29:21.340 --> 00:29:23.240
and wears a sailor's raincoat.

410
00:29:23.280 --> 00:29:25.380
At times when the vessel is in danger,

411
00:29:25.390 --> 00:29:28.500
it will run around the ship and
find some way to warn everyone.

412
00:29:26.720 --> 00:29:27.910
way to warn everyone.

413
00:29:28.520 --> 00:29:31.460
I've heard that they help sailors in other ways, too.

414
00:29:31.490 --> 00:29:35.100
but, to be honest, this is the
first time I've ever heard

415
00:29:35.110 --> 00:29:37.410
someone say outright
that they've seen one.

416
00:29:38.800 --> 00:29:40.700
The more care a ship receives,

417
00:29:40.740 --> 00:29:44.080
the more they grow to
appreciate the sailors.

418
00:29:44.120 --> 00:29:45.680
This ship must've
been determined

419
00:29:45.720 --> 00:29:49.590
to make sure you made it to
the next shore, no matter what.

420
00:29:49.620 --> 00:29:51.260
Just think about it.

421
00:29:51.290 --> 00:29:54.390
This ship had a caring crew that was so special to her.

422
00:29:54.410 --> 00:29:57.280
She even appeared in
human form to reassure them

423
00:29:57.310 --> 00:29:59.080
that everything was
going to be all right.

424
00:29:59.110 --> 00:30:02.350
I bet she's been very happy.

425
00:30:06.960 --> 00:30:08.450
[USOPP]
Merry?

426
00:30:14.470 --> 00:30:18.640
I see. So, it was you.

427
00:30:18.670 --> 00:30:20.470
You were the one
who made those repairs

428
00:30:20.510 --> 00:30:26.080
and spoke to me back then,
weren't you? Merry.

429
00:30:28.840 --> 00:30:32.840
[strong wind]

430
00:30:34.600 --> 00:30:36.600
[landing]

431
00:30:35.720 --> 00:30:39.290
[FRANKY]
As amazing as that is, I'm still confused.

432
00:30:39.320 --> 00:30:43.230
Tell me. Why would you have
a big fight with your crew

433
00:30:43.260 --> 00:30:45.700
when you knew the
ship was done for?

434
00:30:45.740 --> 00:30:47.740
[USOPP sniffling]

435
00:30:47.850 --> 00:30:50.500
[USOPP]
It's not that simple.

436
00:30:50.700 --> 00:30:54.310
I'll never understand why men are so stupid!

437
00:30:54.340 --> 00:30:56.440
Or such idiots!

438
00:30:56.480 --> 00:30:59.360
[KIWI and MOZU crying]

439
00:30:59.490 --> 00:31:03.490
[bell]

440
00:31:04.730 --> 00:31:06.820
[MOZU]
Sounds like someone's at the door.

441
00:31:07.290 --> 00:31:08.290
"Someone"?

442
00:31:08.300 --> 00:31:11.210
[FRANKY]
Who else would it be but Zambai and the others?

443
00:31:11.430 --> 00:31:13.430
[bell]

444
00:31:12.700 --> 00:31:14.530
But why would they
take the long way

445
00:31:14.560 --> 00:31:16.300
and come in from the sea side?

446
00:31:16.360 --> 00:31:18.300
[KIWI]
Yeah, that's odd.

447
00:31:18.330 --> 00:31:20.670
They normally come in through the upper entrance.

448
00:31:20.700 --> 00:31:24.340
Maybe they had to because they
were able to capture Straw Hat?

449
00:31:24.370 --> 00:31:26.670
That's right! I forgot!

450
00:31:26.700 --> 00:31:30.070
I kidnapped you to use you as bait to lure out your crew!

451
00:31:30.110 --> 00:31:31.040
They won't come.

452
00:31:31.080 --> 00:31:33.210
I'm no longer a part
of that crew, remember?

453
00:31:33.210 --> 00:31:35.350
That plan won't work.

454
00:31:38.580 --> 00:31:40.580
[bell]

455
00:31:41.020 --> 00:31:44.460
Why are they ringing the bell when they can just come in?

456
00:31:44.490 --> 00:31:49.300
How annoying. Okay, okay!
Hold on, I'm coming!

457
00:31:49.330 --> 00:31:52.600
Enough, already!
We hear you! Hold on a second!

458
00:31:56.200 --> 00:31:58.470
All right, brother. Listen.

459
00:31:58.470 --> 00:32:03.640
I think what you should do
is go back to your friends.

460
00:32:03.650 --> 00:32:05.350
It's impossible to do that now.

461
00:32:05.380 --> 00:32:07.990
I challenged the captain
to a duel for starters.

462
00:32:08.040 --> 00:32:10.010
And then there's
the matter of the ship

463
00:32:10.040 --> 00:32:11.040
that hasn't been settled yet.

464
00:32:12.640 --> 00:32:14.440
What do you mean
"hasn't been settled"?

465
00:32:14.480 --> 00:32:18.150
If your ship can't sail anymore, then it can't sail anymore.

466
00:32:18.170 --> 00:32:20.170
That's the end of it, right?

467
00:32:23.690 --> 00:32:26.190
Just leave her here with me, okay?

468
00:32:26.220 --> 00:32:28.490
I'll take care of her in a way that you'd approve of.

469
00:32:28.520 --> 00:32:29.560
Problem solved.

470
00:32:29.740 --> 00:32:31.540
I wasn't thinking about what I was doing earlier.

471
00:32:32.060 --> 00:32:34.030
I tried to dismantle the
ship without considering

472
00:32:34.060 --> 00:32:35.100
what would be best for you.

473
00:32:35.130 --> 00:32:36.060
It'll be different this time!

474
00:32:36.360 --> 00:32:39.330
This is my problem!
Stay out of it, okay?!

475
00:32:39.360 --> 00:32:40.600
[FRANKY]
Hey! I'm just trying
to help solve

476
00:32:40.630 --> 00:32:42.670
Is that you, Zambai?

477
00:32:42.710 --> 00:32:44.710
[bell]

478
00:32:44.740 --> 00:32:47.270
[USOPP]
Gratitude? You've
gotta be kidding me!

479
00:32:48.740 --> 00:32:50.740
[FRANKY]
Don't you understand
the situation?!

480
00:32:50.780 --> 00:32:53.510
As hard as it is for you
it's worse on the ship!

481
00:32:53.540 --> 00:32:55.410
She loves you guys so much that

482
00:32:55.450 --> 00:32:56.920
she appeared to
you in human form!

483
00:32:56.940 --> 00:32:58.980
If she sinks to the
bottom of the sea

484
00:32:59.010 --> 00:32:59.980
while you're still on board,

485
00:33:00.010 --> 00:33:02.280
then all of that will
have been for nothing!

486
00:33:02.310 --> 00:33:03.800
Get it? If that happens,

487
00:33:03.800 --> 00:33:05.870
her final moments will
be filled with regret!

488
00:33:05.900 --> 00:33:07.730
She won't be able to die in peace!

489
00:33:07.730 --> 00:33:08.690
Is that what you'd do?

490
00:33:08.730 --> 00:33:09.930
After everything you've
been through together,

491
00:33:09.960 --> 00:33:13.260
you'd leave one of your friends
behind to die on their own?

492
00:33:13.300 --> 00:33:15.270
Just throw them
aside like trash?!

493
00:33:15.280 --> 00:33:17.280
That's not the same thing at all!

494
00:33:17.310 --> 00:33:19.120
This is completely different!

495
00:33:19.150 --> 00:33:22.180
It is the same thing, and that's exactly what's going on!

496
00:33:22.220 --> 00:33:24.650
You just don't get it!

497
00:33:30.390 --> 00:33:32.130
Mozu!

498
00:33:37.200 --> 00:33:40.120
[KALIFA]
I apologize for the interruption.

499
00:33:43.400 --> 00:33:45.670
It's just those two
ladies weren't being

500
00:33:45.710 --> 00:33:49.010
very accommodating
about letting us in.

501
00:33:49.060 --> 00:33:52.160
What the hell are you bastards doing down here?!

502
00:33:55.620 --> 00:33:56.490
Iron Body!

503
00:33:56.520 --> 00:33:59.520
Hey! What's the big idea?

504
00:34:02.590 --> 00:34:03.730
What gives, Blueno?!

505
00:34:03.760 --> 00:34:06.530
You got some kinda
problem with me?!

506
00:34:06.560 --> 00:34:08.660
Oh trying to pull
a reverse move?!

507
00:34:08.750 --> 00:34:12.320
You dumbass, you should
know better than that!

508
00:34:14.480 --> 00:34:16.380
No one pushes me around!

509
00:34:20.820 --> 00:34:23.460
You should be pourin'
me a drink, remember?!

510
00:34:23.460 --> 00:34:25.980
What did you forget
you're just a bartender?

511
00:34:25.980 --> 00:34:28.320
And what's with
that outfit anyway?

512
00:34:28.400 --> 00:34:30.530
What the hell are you up to?!

513
00:34:33.400 --> 00:34:35.270
Not yet!

514
00:34:41.480 --> 00:34:44.920
Whoa! Are you okay?
Come on man, get up!

515
00:34:44.920 --> 00:34:47.390
Killing him now would put our mission in jeopardy.

516
00:34:47.420 --> 00:34:48.460
We need him alive.

517
00:34:48.490 --> 00:34:49.190
Right.

518
00:34:49.190 --> 00:34:50.890
Hey! What's going on here?!

519
00:34:50.950 --> 00:34:54.390
I mean what did you do to piss
off these shipyard guys so bad?

520
00:34:54.420 --> 00:34:55.790
The freak with the bird?

521
00:34:55.950 --> 00:34:57.850
How'd he get a hit
like that on me?!

522
00:34:57.880 --> 00:34:58.680
And what's the deal?

523
00:34:58.720 --> 00:34:59.950
Why're you guys
comin' in on my turf

524
00:35:00.030 --> 00:35:02.970
with a chip on your shoulders,
actin' like you own the place?

525
00:35:03.000 --> 00:35:05.890
And hittin' girls?!
That's so not cool!

526
00:35:05.890 --> 00:35:09.360
Kiwi and Mozu are like my
little sisters, you know?!

527
00:35:09.370 --> 00:35:11.640
How'd you freaks even
find us here anyway?

528
00:35:11.670 --> 00:35:13.800
This is my ultra top secret base!

529
00:35:13.800 --> 00:35:17.310
How we found you's irrelevant
as we are here right now.

530
00:35:17.310 --> 00:35:18.380
But know this.

531
00:35:18.430 --> 00:35:21.240
We came to this town assigned to a covert operation.

532
00:35:21.270 --> 00:35:22.740
We're special agents...

533
00:35:22.770 --> 00:35:25.710
spies working for the
world government.

534
00:35:25.710 --> 00:35:27.550
I assume even you
would know why

535
00:35:27.580 --> 00:35:30.980
we came here and
what we're after.

536
00:35:31.020 --> 00:35:34.850
Franky, we know the secret that you're keeping.

537
00:35:34.920 --> 00:35:36.850
Cutty Flam.

538
00:35:36.900 --> 00:35:38.900
The rumor was that
Tom's apprentice

539
00:35:38.980 --> 00:35:41.710
perished about eight years ago.

540
00:35:41.740 --> 00:35:45.350
But you're still alive.

541
00:35:45.420 --> 00:35:47.620
That's some pretty amazing detective work.

542
00:35:47.670 --> 00:35:49.440
I'm real impressed.

543
00:35:49.470 --> 00:35:53.480
But I'm startin' to get a
sour feeling down in my gut.

544
00:35:53.510 --> 00:35:56.710
Where is he? Where
the hell is Iceburg?

545
00:35:56.740 --> 00:35:58.350
He's dead.

546
00:36:00.420 --> 00:36:03.360
It's too late to feign innocence.

547
00:36:03.390 --> 00:36:05.290
We already know everything.

548
00:36:07.230 --> 00:36:08.500
It's only a matter of time

549
00:36:08.530 --> 00:36:10.060
before the
government targets me.

550
00:36:10.100 --> 00:36:14.030
I want you to take these
and leave the island, Franky.

551
00:36:14.030 --> 00:36:16.700
Tom entrusted them to Iceburg

552
00:36:16.830 --> 00:36:20.500
and Iceburg
entrusted them to you.

553
00:36:20.540 --> 00:36:22.810
Hey, boys, come here.

554
00:36:22.840 --> 00:36:25.480
It's about time I let you
in on somethin' important!

555
00:36:25.540 --> 00:36:29.280
It's been a long game but
now we're at checkmate.

556
00:36:29.410 --> 00:36:33.250
See, I know you have the plans for the ancient weapon.

557
00:36:33.260 --> 00:36:37.240
Hand over Pluton's
blueprints, Cutty Flam.

558
00:36:37.270 --> 00:36:40.070
Flam, huh? That's
kind of a funny name.

559
00:36:40.120 --> 00:36:42.630
How about we just call you Franky instead?

560
00:36:42.660 --> 00:36:44.360
Whatever.

561
00:36:44.380 --> 00:36:46.440
Are you listening?

562
00:36:46.480 --> 00:36:49.850
Hand them over this instant.

563
00:36:50.600 --> 00:36:53.470
Oh, did you say hand?

564
00:37:05.000 --> 00:37:07.400
What the hell did he just do?

565
00:37:07.400 --> 00:37:09.970
It was so fast I couldn't
see what happened.

566
00:37:10.560 --> 00:37:12.880
Hey! Are you okay?!

567
00:37:18.240 --> 00:37:20.040
Oh my.

568
00:37:20.080 --> 00:37:21.580
You found a room.

569
00:37:21.590 --> 00:37:25.130
What do you suppose is this filthy place's purpose?

570
00:37:25.160 --> 00:37:26.900
Those are drafting tables.

571
00:37:26.930 --> 00:37:32.800
Yes. Where blueprints are made
and perhaps hidden. Find them!

572
00:37:42.280 --> 00:37:50.120
Look here, nameplates.
Cutty Flam. Iceburg. Tom.

573
00:37:50.140 --> 00:37:52.270
The shipwright.

574
00:37:54.040 --> 00:37:56.910
This picture.

575
00:37:56.990 --> 00:38:01.360
Keep your paws off of that!

576
00:38:01.390 --> 00:38:04.530
You're pokin' your noses
into my personal space.

577
00:38:04.560 --> 00:38:09.470
My memories! This is the
place where I grew up.

578
00:38:09.500 --> 00:38:12.100
What used to house the
shipbuilding company,

579
00:38:12.140 --> 00:38:14.100
Tom's Workers.
Where the best
